From: GertaBool <67003432+GertaBool@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 15:35:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Graphics-Paging-Fix-Test (8587217): paging selection, diplomacy valuation, and callback define fixes

Cumulative patch over GitLab Graphics-Paging-Fix-Test 8587217eeb94:
1. Graphics paging selection restoration, multi-selected cities, and bulk-reveal routes
   (CvGame.cpp, CvCity.cpp, CvGameInterface.cpp, CvDLLButtonPopup.cpp, CvPlot.cpp).
2. AI_counterPropose false rejections, 64-bit gold/GPT overflow, AI-AI strictly positive
   swap gains, and AI_DIPLOMACY_NET_VALUE flag contract
   (AIDiplomacyPolicy.h, CvGameCoreUtils.h, CvPlayerAI.cpp, BBAI_AI_Variables_GlobalDefines.xml).
3. USE_CANNOT_SPREAD_RELIGION_CALLBACK define typo in CvGlobals::cacheGlobals
   (CvGlobals.cpp).

Serves: P15
---
diff --git a/Assets/CvGameCoreDLL/AIDiplomacyPolicy.h b/Assets/CvGameCoreDLL/AIDiplomacyPolicy.h
index 9bc2bf8..4c48a8b 100644
--- a/Assets/CvGameCoreDLL/AIDiplomacyPolicy.h
+++ b/Assets/CvGameCoreDLL/AIDiplomacyPolicy.h
@@ -53,6 +53,55 @@ inline int saturatingAdd(int left, int right)
 	const long long sum = (long long)left + right;
 	return sum < INT_MIN ? INT_MIN : (sum > INT_MAX ? INT_MAX : (int)sum);
 }
+
+// Payer cost of a gold-per-turn commitment over ``horizon`` turns. Payments
+// covered by net income or spendable treasury above ``goldTarget`` keep their
+// ordinary value; uncovered GPT scales up to 2x to reflect deficit/strike risk.
+inline int goldPerTurnCostVal(int goldPerTurn, int goldValuePercent, int horizon,
+	int goldRate, int gold, int goldTarget)
+{
+	if (goldPerTurn <= 0 || goldValuePercent <= 0)
+	{
+		return 0;
+	}
+	const int iHorizon = (horizon > 0) ? horizon : 1;
+	const int iBaseCost = valueFromGold(goldPerTurn, goldValuePercent * iHorizon);
+	const long long iSpendableGold = (long long)gold - goldTarget;
+	const long long iSustainablePayment = ((goldRate > 0) ? (long long)goldRate : (long long)0) +
+		((iSpendableGold > 0) ? (iSpendableGold / iHorizon) : (long long)0);
+	const int iUncoveredPayment = (iSustainablePayment >= goldPerTurn) ? 0 :
+		(goldPerTurn - (int)iSustainablePayment);
+	const long long iCost = (long long)iBaseCost +
+		(((long long)iBaseCost * iUncoveredPayment) / goldPerTurn);
+	return iCost > INT_MAX ? INT_MAX : (int)iCost;
+}
+
+// Largest GPT in [0, maxGoldPerTurn] whose payer cost satisfies (< maxValue)
+// when strictLess is true, or (<= maxValue) when strictLess is false.
+inline int maxAffordableGoldPerTurn(int maxValue, int maxGoldPerTurn, int goldValuePercent,
+	int horizon, int goldRate, int gold, int goldTarget, bool strictLess)
+{
+	if (maxValue <= 0 || maxGoldPerTurn <= 0 || goldValuePercent <= 0)
+	{
+		return 0;
+	}
+	int iLow = 0;
+	int iHigh = maxGoldPerTurn;
+	while (iLow < iHigh)
+	{
+		const int iMiddle = iLow + ((iHigh - iLow) / 2) + ((iHigh - iLow) % 2);
+		const int iCost = goldPerTurnCostVal(iMiddle, goldValuePercent, horizon, goldRate, gold, goldTarget);
+		if (strictLess ? (iCost < maxValue) : (iCost <= maxValue))
+		{
+			iLow = iMiddle;
+		}
+		else
+		{
+			iHigh = iMiddle - 1;
+		}
+	}
+	return iLow;
+}
 }
 
 #endif
